$\begin{aligned} & \mathrm{AX}=\mathrm{B} \\ \therefore \quad & {\left[\begin{array}{ccc}1 & -1 & 2 \\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\ 3 & 2 & 1\end{array}\right]\left[\begin{array}{l}\mathrm{a} \\ \mathrm{b} \\ \mathrm{c}\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{l}3 \\ 1 \\ 4\end{array}\right] }\end{aligned}\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore \quad & a-b+2 c=3 ...(i)\\
& 2 a+c=1...(ii) \\
& 3 a+2 b+c=4
...(iii)\end{array}
Solving (i), (ii) and (iii), we get
\begin{aligned}$& a=-1, b=2, c=3 \\
\therefore \quad 2 a-3 b+4 c & =2(-1)-3(2)+4(3) \\
& =4
\end{aligned}
